# Binary assets must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
#
# This repo is checked out with core.autocrlf=true. Every background video was
# committed with each CRLF collapsed to a bare LF, which shifted every byte
# offset after the first loss: Chrome then decoded three to ten frames of a
# hundred and froze, which is what "the videos shake" was. Git's own binary
# heuristic did not save them, so the file types are declared here instead.
#
# Verify after any media change:  python -s scripts/check-site.py

*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.webm  binary
*.m4v   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.zip   binary

# Deliberately nothing here for text. HTML in this repo is a mix of CRLF
# (index.html, industries.html, industries/*.html) and LF (assets/*, the rest),
# and declaring an eol would renormalize every one of them into a whole-file
# diff. Edits preserve each file's existing endings instead.
